I am not recommending on using them before reaching the mid
game. Actually you should use only the poisoned ones that you
find, because they cannot be merged with the rest.

They are good from the mid-game once you can enchant them.

I think you are underestimating darts. The difference in base
damage is only 2 points. You seem to be discounting that
darts at expert can be thrown thrice, making the average
damage exactly double, compared to the 1.5 times at
skilled. So at expert +7 darts with max strength will do 33
points of damage while skilled daggers in similar situation
will do only 17.5*1.5=26.25 damage, which is quite less.
Even if you use strength at 18. The damage difference will
be 25 for +7 darts and 20.5.

But the real killer is the weight. With darts you can just fire
away and pick them when all opponents are dead, or you
think you can waste a turn. With Daggers you run out of
your inventory very fast.

They are a real substitute for Magic Missiles. They do
nearly the same damage at lower XL. And they will last
longer than your mana unless you have the Eye.

The ability for them to be poisoned makes them even
more deadly.

The thing is that with maxed luck and blessed +7 darts you don't
really need more than 50 darts for the complete game, if you
don't loose some on the watery planes.

I prefer them over arrows because they also don't require
you to carry a bow. And unless you are a elf/orc/samurai
firing their special type of arrows with their type of bows,
the strength damage makes them superior.

I will be carrying the quest bow just to be able to fire the 9
silver arrows (at the major demons), that I found in the shop.
I might even wish for 20 more. If I do wish and get about 29
then they will be used against all silver hating creatures.
29 should last easily the whole of gehennom, at 5800
possible hits.

